  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Why milk leaves you bloated and running to the bathroom",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Your small intestine uses",
        "an enzyme called lactase",
        "to break down lactose",
        "",
        "Without enough of it, lactose",
        "reaches your colon undigested",
        "and gut bacteria ferment it",
        "into gas, cramping, diarrhea",
        "",
        "The NIH estimates 30 to 50",
        "million Americans deal with it —",
        "far more in some groups"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "It hits some groups much harder",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Up to 90% of Asian Americans",
        "and 80% of Black Americans",
        "have lactose intolerance",
        "",
        "Compared to as little as 15%",
        "of people with Northern",
        "European ancestry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Choose the right dairy",
      "char_file": "치즈_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Fresh milk keeps its",
        "lactose fully intact",
        "",
        "Hard, aged cheeses like cheddar,",
        "parmesan, and gouda test under",
        "0.1g of lactose per serving"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "How you eat it matters",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Your body can only break down",
        "so much lactose at once",
        "",
        "A full glass on an empty",
        "stomach overwhelms it fast"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Change your eating pattern like this",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Spread dairy across the day,",
        "pair it with other food,",
        "skip drinking it on an empty stomach"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Replace the missing enzyme",
      "char_file": "알약_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Lactase supplements supply",
        "the enzyme your gut",
        "isn't making enough of"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Use supplements like this",
      "char_file": "알약_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Take 1 to 3 caplets right",
        "with your first bite of dairy —",
        "each dose covers about 30 to 45 minutes"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      [
        "Switch up the type of dairy",
        "and how you eat it"
      ],
      [
        "and lactose intolerance",
        "gets a lot easier to live with"
      ]
    ],
    "tip": [
      "Start with Greek yogurt or an aged cheese, and spread milk across meals instead of one big glass",
      "Unexplained weight loss or blood in your stool points to something beyond lactose intolerance — see a doctor"
    ],
